#N canvas 20 20 1900 1400 12;
#X text 20 20 m_launchpad -- the Launchpad Pro MK3's device layer \, and the only file that talks to it: Programmer Mode \, the safe exit and the replug watchdog \, so everything that changes what the surface is lives in one place. Pads \, ring \, pressure and a tap on Setup go out as named controls on param \, with no notion of what they do. ref/device/launchpad.md, f 58;
#X text 20 190 creation arg 1: the Pd channel the Launchpad's own channel 1 lands on (1 on the device) \, required. inlet: a bang from u_init at the Launchpad stage. outlet 1: surface ownership \, 1 while the device is in Programmer Mode and its LEDs are ours \, 0 when the watchdog loses it or the safe exit hands it back. Wired to g_grid., f 58;
#X text 900 170 The block doubles as the output port: the init's literal 1 and the watchdog's \$1 \, like g_grid's \, assume the Launchpad is input slot 1 and output port 1 (ref/architecture.md \, Creation arguments)., f 58;
#X obj 20 520 inlet;
#N canvas 40 40 1400 760 init 0;
#X text 20 20 Startup: Programmer Mode \, then ownership. No grid clear here: LED state survives the mode switch \, and g_grid's first frame after ownership paints all 108 indices \, which is the clear., f 58;
#X obj 20 260 inlet;
#X obj 20 320 t b b b b;
#X msg 20 400 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 14 \, 1 \, 247;
#X obj 20 480 midiout;
#X obj 700 260 loadbang;
#X msg 700 320 1;
#X msg 1000 480 1;
#X obj 1000 540 s \$0-own;
#X text 700 620 The port goes into the cold inlet at load: Pd 0.49 does not warn about an extra creation argument \, so a [midiout 1] would prove nothing., f 50;
#X text 20 580 The trigger orders it: want \, then the expected echo \, then Programmer Mode \, then ownership \, which starts g_grid painting and so must not come while the device is in Live Mode. The echo is the setup subpatch's: entering Programmer Mode makes the device announce it \, as a tap on Setup does., f 58;
