#X msg 1300 400 1;
#X obj 1300 460 s \$0-want;
#X text 1300 520 want is not own: own says the surface is ours \, want that we still intend it to be. The watchdog's heartbeat re-asserts Programmer Mode while want is 1 \, and only the safe exit drops it., f 50;
#X connect 2 3 11 0;
#X connect 11 0 12 0;
#X obj 1000 400 s \$0-entered;
#X connect 2 2 14 0;
#X restore 20 600 pd init;
#N canvas 40 40 1200 900 safe-exit 0;
#X text 20 20 Back to Live Mode on quit only: Programmer Mode by SysEx locks out the device's Settings menu \, so the surface must be handed back before Pd goes or the front panel cannot recover it., f 60;
#X text 20 140 quitting is the only shutdown hook \, with about 100 ms before Pd quits: enough for one SysEx (ref/conventions.md)., f 58;
#X obj 20 430 r quitting;
#X obj 20 480 t b b b;
#X msg 700 560 1;
#X msg 300 560 240 \, 0 \, 32 \, 41 \, 2 \, 14 \, 14 \, 0 \, 247;
#X obj 300 660 midiout;
#X text 20 700 No grid clear here: Live Mode redraws the surface \, and the 100 ms goes to the one message that matters., f 58;
#X msg 940 300 0;
#X obj 940 360 s \$0-own;
#X obj 1250 360 s \$0-want;
#X text 20 1000 Do not wire r panic in here. A panic that hands the surface back sets want 0 \, so the grid stays dead until a reload \, and in Live Mode the device floods Pd's Midi-In 1 with clock (items 250 and 251)., f 60;
