#X text 20 1030 The two decodes run opposite ways because the outlet orders do (item 23): notein's pitch fires last \, so it triggers and the velocity is stored \, and ctlin's value fires last \, so its number is stored. Hence t b f for pads and t f b for the ring., f 58;
#X text 700 780 Names are physical: pads by position (pad-43) \, the ring by its CC number (lp-cc-91)., f 58;
#X text 700 940 A release is velocity 0 \, so a pad publishes twice per hit. What a press means \, and whether the release matters \, is u_map's., f 58;
