#N canvas 40 40 2000 1560 setup 0;
#X text 20 20 The Setup button \, the bottom left corner. In Programmer Mode a tap sends nothing on port 0 \, but the device announces its layout on port 2 \, the frame 240 0 32 41 2 14 0 17 0 0 247 \, which wire.sh joins to Midi-In 1 \; a hold sends nothing at all. Entering Programmer Mode while in it announces the same frame \, once \, within a millisecond \, so the init and the heartbeat each expect an echo before they send \, and an announcement nothing expected is a tap: lp-setup 127 on param \, as a ring button's press. There is no release to publish. ref/device/launchpad.md, f 70;
#X text 700 20 The match \, three rules: F0 resets the index and sets the match \, every byte must equal the frame's at its index \, past its end included \, or the match is cleared \, and F7 bangs a match still standing and then clears it. 247 ends this frame and appears nowhere else in it \, so a frame of another length cannot match. Realtime bytes are dropped \, as in c_devid., f 60;
#X text 1400 20 An expected echo is forgotten 250 ms after the last entry: the device echoes within a millisecond \, and one it never sent must not swallow a later tap. A tap inside those 250 ms whose echo was lost is the price. t f f keeps the count in both stores \, one number read from two places (C-13: no value)., f 50;
